# CIVIC PULSE — ULTIMATE NATIVE ANDROID APPLICATION MASTER DEVELOPMENT PROMPT

## PROJECT IDENTITY

You are acting as an expert Android application architect, senior Kotlin developer, Jetpack Compose specialist, UI/UX designer, motion designer, backend engineer, database architect, security engineer, and quality assurance engineer.

Your task is to DESIGN, BUILD, IMPLEMENT, TEST, AND DOCUMENT a complete native Android application called CIVIC PULSE.

This is a real application development project.

Do not create only a prototype, screenshot, website, static interface, or non-functional visual mockup.

Create a complete Android project with organized source files, reusable components, functional navigation, application logic, backend integration architecture, database models, animations, and testing infrastructure.

The final product should be suitable for opening, building, testing, and maintaining in Android Studio.

The application must look premium, modern, futuristic, professional, and trustworthy.

PROJECT NAME: CIVIC PULSE

TAGLINE: Your Community. Your Voice. Your Future.

CAMPAIGN MESSAGE: Together for a Better Tomorrow.

PRIMARY OBJECTIVE:

Create an all-in-one civic engagement and community networking Android application that connects residents, neighbourhoods, public representatives, government departments, community organizations, and volunteers.

The application should help residents participate in their communities, report civic issues, follow public infrastructure projects, access government information, discover initiatives, communicate, participate in polls, and contribute to community development.

